On Fri, Dec 23, 2011 at 2:58 PM, Robin Lee Powell
<rlpowell@digitalkingdom.org> wrote:
>
> i.e., can PEG support having one set of fore logical connectives
> only, or is the issue deeper than lookahead?

If the question is whether guheks can be replaced by geks, then the
answer is no, because tanru "gu'e broda gi brode" is different from
bridi "ge broda gi brode". Compare "(gu'e broda gi brode) ko'a" with
"ge (broda) gi (brode ko'a)".

If the question is whether guheks would be missed by anyone if they
were just dropped, then probably not. I don't think anyone ever uses
them.

